<h2 class="mdr-overview-label">Overview</h2>
 <p class="mdr-overview-intro">Security tools raise alerts; someone still has to read them at 3 am, decide what&#39;s real and act. Most businesses can&#39;t staff that \u2014 five or more analysts for round-the-clock cover \u2014 and attackers know it. XcellHost MDR is that team, as a service. We monitor 24\xD77\xD7365, investigate with telemetry, threat intelligence and forensics, respond immediately to contain threats, and \u2014 because it runs on Acronis Cyber Protect Cloud \u2014 recover affected data and patch the gap as part of the same incident.</p>
 <div class="pp-answer" id="answer">
  <div><span class="kick">QUICK ANSWER \xB7 UPDATED SEPTEMBER 2026</span><h2>What is managed detection and response (MDR)?</h2><p data-speakable>Managed detection and response (MDR) is a 24\xD77\xD7365 service in which a security operations centre (SOC) team monitors your environment, investigates suspicious activity and responds to threats on your behalf \u2014 containing, remediating and reporting, not just forwarding alerts. XcellHost MDR runs on Acronis EDR/XDR, so response can also include rolling back ransomware changes and restoring data from backup. It is offered in Standard and Advanced tiers and billed per protected workload in INR.</p></div>
  <div><span class="kick">KEY TAKEAWAYS</span><ul><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>MDR is an outsourced SOC: people who act, not just software that alerts</span></li><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Round-the-clock cover in-house usually needs five or more analysts</span></li><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Analysts investigate and contain \u2014 traditional MSSPs mostly forward alerts</span></li><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Integrated backup lets response include rollback and recovery</span></li><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Standard for containment and guidance; Advanced for full remediation and hunting</span></li></ul>
   <div class="bestfor"><span>Best for:</span><b>SMBs without a SOC</b><b>Mid-market IT teams</b><b>Regulated industries</b><b>Cyber-insurance requirements</b></div></div>
