    args: [{ selector: "xh-rtx-pro-6000-showcase", standalone: true, changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy22.OnPush, template: '<section class="rtx-use-cases" aria-label="RTX PRO 6000 use cases and supported platforms">\n<h2 class="pp-sec">Use cases</h2>\n <div class="pp-feats"><div class="pp-feat"><span class="ic"><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 4a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-2 5 3 3 0 0 0 2 5 3 3 0 0 0 3 3 3 3 0 0 0 3-3V7a3 3 0 0 0-3-3z"/><path d="M15 4a3 3 0 0 1 3 3 3 3 0 0 1 2 5 3 3 0 0 1-2 5 3 3 0 0 1-3 3 3 3 0 0 1-3-3"/></svg></span><p><b>LLM fine-tuning &amp; inference</b>LoRA/QLoRA on 7B\u201370B models; high-throughput serving with vLLM or TensorRT-LLM.</p></div><div class="pp-feat"><span class="ic"><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M7 4v16M17 4v16M3 9h4M3 15h4M17 9h4M17 15h4"/></svg></span><p><b>Generative video &amp; images</b>Text-to-video, diffusion and upscaling pipelines that need memory headroom.</p></div><div class="pp-feat"><span class="ic"><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 2 9 5v10l-9 5-9-5V7z"/><path d="m3 7 9 5 9-5M12 12v10"/></svg></span><p><b>Heavy 3D &amp; digital twins</b>Omniverse, Unreal and USD scenes too large for 48 GB cards.</p></div><div class="pp-feat"><span class="ic"><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"/><path d="m12 8 1.5 2.5L16 12l-2.5 1.5L12 16l-1.5-2.5L8 12l2.5-1.5z"/></svg></span><p><b>Rendering &amp; VFX</b>Path-traced frames for studios in Mumbai, Hyderabad and Pune without a render farm.</p></div><div class="pp-feat"><span class="ic"><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 3h6M10 3v6L4 19a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.3 2h13.4A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 20 19l-6-10V3"/><path d="M7 15h10"/></svg></span><p><b>Simulation &amp; science</b>CFD, molecular dynamics and geospatial workloads with FP32 muscle.</p></div><div class="pp-feat"><span class="ic"><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 20V10M10 20V4M16 20v-7M22 20H2"/></svg></span><p><b>Analytics on GPU</b>RAPIDS, cuDF and vector search over large in-memory datasets.</p></div><div class="pp-feat"><span class="ic"><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="8" r="3.5"/><path d="M2 20c0-4 3-6 7-6s7 2 7 6"/><path d="M16 4.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7M18 14c2.5.6 4 2.6 4 6"/></svg></span><p><b>Shared team workstations</b>MIG slices or vWS desktops for design and data-science teams.</p></div></div>\n\n <h2 class="pp-sec">Platforms &amp; workloads covered</h2>\n <div class="tiles"><div ><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M3 12h18M12 4v16"/></svg>Windows Server</div><div ><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3c-2.5 0-3.5 2-3.5 5 0 2-2 4-3 7-.5 2 1 4 3 4h7c2 0 3.5-2 3-4-1-3-3-5-3-7 0-3-1-5-3.5-5z"/><path d="M10 8h.01M14 8h.01"/></svg>Ubuntu Linux</div><div ><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 3 9 5-9 5-9-5z"/><path d="m3 13 9 5 9-5"/></svg>Docker</div><div ><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 2 9 5v10l-9 5-9-5V7z"/><path d="m3 7 9 5 9-5M12 12v10"/></svg>Kubernetes</div><div ><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m8 8-5 4 5 4M16 8l5 4-5 4M14 5l-4 14"/></svg>Jupyter</div><div ><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M3 12h18M12 3a14 14 0 0 1 0 18M12 3a14 14 0 0 0 0 18"/></svg>Any browser (RDP/DCV)</div></div>\n\n \n</section>\n<section class="rtx-stories" aria-label="RTX PRO 6000 case studies and GPU comparison">\n<h2 class="pp-sec" id="cases">Case studies \u2014 what teams achieve</h2>\n <div class="cases"><article class="case">\n  <div class="case-hd"><span class="case-av">LF</span><div><h3>Moving a document-AI model from US GPUs to India cut latency and settled data-residency questions</h3><small>Lending fintech, 120 staff \xB7 Fintech \xB7 Bengaluru<span class="case-tag">Illustrative case study</span></small></div></div>\n  <div class="case-body">\n   <div><h4>Challenge</h4><p>The team served a 34B-parameter document-understanding model on US-hosted GPUs. Round-trip latency from India was high, egress bills were unpredictable, and the compliance team wanted borrower data kept in India under the DPDP Act.</p></div>\n   <div><h4>What we set up</h4><p>Two XG.PRO6K.1-32 instances in our Mumbai zone running vLLM with FP8 weights, a private network to their app servers, and MIG slices for staging. We migrated weights and set up Grafana GPU dashboards.</p><p class="case-plan">Configuration: <b>2 \xD7 XG.PRO6K.1-32 on a 12-month term</b></p></div>\n   <div class="case-res"><div><b data-count="62" data-pre="" data-suf="%">62%</b><span>lower p95 inference latency</span></div><div><b data-count="38" data-pre="" data-suf="%">38%</b><span>lower monthly GPU bill in INR</span></div><div><b data-count="100" data-pre="" data-suf="%">100%</b><span>borrower data kept in India</span></div></div>\n  </div></article><article class="case">\n  <div class="case-hd"><span class="case-av">AP</span><div><h3>Generative video previz for ad agencies without building a render farm</h3><small>Ad-film post studio \xB7 Media \xB7 Mumbai<span class="case-tag">Illustrative case study</span></small></div></div>\n  <div class="case-body">\n   <div><h4>Challenge</h4><p>Agencies wanted AI-generated animatics within a day. The studio&#39;s 24 GB workstations ran out of memory on text-to-video models, so jobs failed or had to be cut into short clips.</p></div>\n   <div><h4>What we set up</h4><p>A 4-GPU XG.PRO6K.4-96 node with ComfyUI and a shared NVMe project volume. Artists queue jobs from their desks; we burst to hourly billing during campaign weeks.</p><p class="case-plan">Configuration: <b>1 \xD7 XG.PRO6K.4-96, hourly during peaks</b></p></div>\n   <div class="case-res"><div><b data-count="3" data-pre="" data-suf="\xD7">3\xD7</b><span>more concepts delivered per brief</span></div><div><b data-count="18" data-pre="" data-suf=" h">18 h</b><span>turnaround, down from 3 days</span></div><div><b data-count="0" data-pre="" data-suf="">0</b><span>out-of-memory failures after migration</span></div></div>\n  </div></article><article class="case">\n  <div class="case-hd"><span class="case-av">AM</span><div><h3>A plant digital twin that engineers and the AI team share on one GPU pool</h3><small>Auto-components maker \xB7 Manufacturing \xB7 Pune<span class="case-tag">Illustrative case study</span></small></div></div>\n  <div class="case-body">\n   <div><h4>Challenge</h4><p>Engineering needed a real-time Omniverse twin of a new line, while the data team trained vision models for defect detection. Buying separate workstations and a training server would take a full quarter&#39;s budget.</p></div>\n   <div><h4>What we set up</h4><p>Two XG.PRO6K.2-64 nodes: MIG slices for vision training during the day, full GPUs for the twin during design reviews. A site-to-site VPN connects the plant network.</p><p class="case-plan">Configuration: <b>2 \xD7 XG.PRO6K.2-64 on a 6-month term</b></p></div>\n   <div class="case-res"><div><b data-count="41" data-pre="" data-suf="%">41%</b><span>faster line-commissioning sign-off</span></div><div><b data-count="2" data-pre="" data-suf="">2</b><span>teams sharing one GPU budget</span></div><div><b data-count="55" data-pre="" data-suf="%">55%</b><span>lower cost than buying workstations</span></div></div>\n  </div></article></div>\n\n <h2 class="pp-sec">Compare professional GPUs</h2>\n <div class="gsw"><a class="gcard cur" href="/rtx-pro-6000"><span class="badge">YOU ARE HERE</span>\n  <div class="img">\n<svg class="gc" viewBox="0 0 640 300" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of the NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell graphics card">\n <defs>\n  