  <div><span class="kick">QUICK ANSWER \xB7 UPDATED SEPTEMBER 2026</span><h2>Do you need to back up Microsoft 365?</h2><p data-speakable>Yes. Under Microsoft&#39;s shared responsibility model, Microsoft keeps the Microsoft 365 service available, but the data inside it \u2014 mail, files, sites and chats \u2014 is the customer&#39;s responsibility, and the Microsoft Services Agreement recommends customers regularly back up their content. Native recycle bins and retention settings keep deleted items only for limited windows that depend on the workload and licence, and they live in the same tenant as the data they protect. A third-party Microsoft 365 backup keeps independent, encrypted, immutable copies with retention you set, and restores individual items or whole users to any point in time.</p></div>\r
  <div><span class="kick">KEY TAKEAWAYS</span><ul><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Microsoft keeps the service up; protecting the data is on you</span></li><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Recycle bins and retention expire on a timer and live in the same tenant</span></li><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Ransomware, departing staff and admin mistakes are the everyday causes of loss</span></li><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Point-in-time, item-level restore beats rebuilding from scratch</span></li><li><svg class="xg-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Immutable copies outside the tenant are what make recovery certain</span></li></ul>\r
   <div class="bestfor"><span>Best for:</span><b>Microsoft 365 businesses</b><b>IT teams &amp; MSPs</b><b>Regulated industries</b><b>Firms with staff turnover</b></div></div>\r
 </div>\r
